      "kind": "yearly",
      "fiscal_year": 2023,
      "summary": {
        "headline": "In fiscal year 2023, most household mail categories saw declines from the previous year and five years earlier, though packages decreased from 2022 but increased from 2018.",
        "statements": [
          {
            "text": "Advertising mail received by households was 57286.0 millions of pieces in fiscal year 2023, a decrease of 8033.0 millions of pieces (12.3%) from 2022, and a decrease of 17989.0 millions of pieces (23.9%) from 2018.",
            "metric": "advertising-received-total",
            "years": [
              2023,
              2022,
              2018
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The share of bills paid by mail was 15.0 percent in fiscal year 2023, which is 2.0 percent lower than in 2022 and 12.0 percent lower than in 2018.",
            "metric": "bills-paid-by-mail-share",
            "years": [
              2023,
              2022,
              2018
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Households received 32228.0 millions of pieces of First-Class Mail in fiscal year 2023, a decline of 1319.0 millions of pieces (3.9%) from 2022 and 6730.0 millions of pieces (17.3%) from 2018.",
            "metric": "fcm-received-total",
            "years": [
              2023,
              2022,
              2018
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Total household mail, including sent and received pieces, was 97400.0 millions of pieces in fiscal year 2023, an 8500.0 millions of pieces (8.0%) decrease from 2022 and a 23600.0 millions of pieces (19.5%) decrease from 2018.",
            "metric": "household-mail-total",
            "years": [
              2023,
              2022,
              2018
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Packages sent and received by households totaled 6700.0 millions of pieces in fiscal year 2023, a decrease of 600.0 millions of pieces (8.2%) from 2022, but an increase of 1400.0 millions of pieces (26.4%) from 2018.",
            "metric": "packages-volume",
            "years": [
              2023,
              2022,
              2018
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Periodicals received by households were 3400.0 millions of pieces in fiscal year 2023, an increase of 100.0 millions of pieces (3.0%) from 2022, but a decrease of 1000.0 millions of pieces (22.7%) from 2018.",
            "metric": "periodicals-volume",
            "years": [
              2023,
              2022,
              2018
            ]
          }
        ],
        "caveats": [
          "From the FY2024 report, results for 2014-2023 were restated on a new basis due to a change in the survey contractor and reporting as pieces per household per year, so comparisons across this break should be made cautiously.",
          "The Household Mail Survey will undergo a redesign in FY2025, including changes to age bands and the definition of 'Large MSA', which may affect future comparisons."
        ]
      },
