        "headline": "Household mail usage shows mixed trends with overall declines, while packages are projected to increase.",
        "statements": [
          {
            "text": "Advertising mail received by households (advertising-received-total) decreased by -20084.0 million pieces (-26.0%) from 2000 to 2023, and by -17989.0 million pieces (-23.9%) over the last 5 years (2018-2023). From 2022 to 2023, this metric decreased by -8033.0 million pieces and is projected to continue decreasing from 57286.0 million pieces in 2023 to 49387.0 million pieces in 2028, with an 80% confidence range of 38755.0 to 60019.0 million pieces for 2028; this projection beats the naive baseline.",
            "metric": "advertising-received-total",
            "years": [
              2000,
              2023,
              2018,
              2022,
              2028
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The share of bills paid by mail (bills-paid-by-mail-share) decreased by -67.0 percentage points from 2000 to 2025, and by -17.0 percentage points over the last 10 years (2015-2025). From 2024 to 2025, this metric increased by 1.0 percentage point, but is projected to decrease from 14.0 percent in 2025 to 3.0 percent in 2030, with an 80% confidence range of 0.0 to 9.6 percent for 2030; this projection beats the naive baseline.",
            "metric": "bills-paid-by-mail-share",
            "years": [
              2000,
              2025,
              2015,
              2024,
              2030
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "First-Class Mail received by households (fcm-received-total) decreased by -24577.0 million pieces (-43.3%) from 2000 to 2023, and by -6730.0 million pieces (-17.3%) over the last 5 years (2018-2023). From 2022 to 2023, this metric decreased by -1319.0 million pieces and is projected to continue decreasing from 32228.0 million pieces in 2023 to 25368.0 million pieces in 2028, with an 80% confidence range of 23270.0 to 27467.0 million pieces for 2028; this projection beats the naive baseline.",
            "metric": "fcm-received-total",
            "years": [
              2000,
              2023,
              2018,
              2022,
              2028
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "All household mail, sent and received (household-mail-total), decreased by -60900.0 million pieces (-38.5%) from 2003 to 2023, and by -36500.0 million pieces (-27.3%) over the last 10 years (2013-2023). From 2022 to 2023, this metric decreased by -8500.0 million pieces and is projected to continue decreasing from 97400.0 million pieces in 2023 to 79445.0 million pieces in 2028, with an 80% confidence range of 65020.0 to 93871.0 million pieces for 2028; this projection beats the naive baseline.",
            "metric": "household-mail-total",
            "years": [
              2003,
              2023,
              2013,
              2022,
              2028
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Packages sent and received by households (packages-volume) increased by 4100.0 million pieces (157.7%) from 2003 to 2023, and by 2600.0 million pieces (63.4%) over the last 10 years (2013-2023). From 2022 to 2023, this metric decreased by -600.0 million pieces, but is projected to increase from 6700.0 million pieces in 2023 to 8550.0 million pieces in 2028, with an 80% confidence range of 6786.0 to 10314.0 million pieces for 2028; this projection beats the naive baseline.",
            "metric": "packages-volume",
            "years": [
              2003,
              2023,
              2013,
              2022,
              2028
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Periodicals received by households (periodicals-volume) decreased by -3400.0 million pieces (-50.0%) from 2003 to 2023, and by -1000.0 million pieces (-22.7%) over the last 5 years (2018-2023). From 2022 to 2023, this metric increased by 100.0 million pieces, but is projected to decrease from 3400.0 million pieces in 2023 to 2023.0 million pieces in 2028, with an 80% confidence range of 1546.0 to 2500.0 million pieces for 2028; this projection beats the naive baseline.",
            "metric": "periodicals-volume",
            "years": [
              2003,
              2023,
              2018,
              2022,
              2028
            ]
          }
        ],
        "caveats": [
